# ERD §15.3 — Desktop Google OAuth client credentials.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values from a Google
# Cloud Console OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Desktop app".
#
# The PWA's existing Web client (used for GIS implicit flow) does
# NOT work for the desktop loopback flow — Google's OAuth
# implementation rejects the Desktop redirect_uri pattern from a
# Web-type client. You need to create a separate "Desktop app" client.
#
# Setup:
#
#   1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#      (under your existing DayRail project).
#   2. Click "Create Credentials" → "OAuth client ID".
#   3. Application type: "Desktop app". Name: "DayRail Desktop".
#   4. Click Create. Copy both values into .env.
#
# Per RFC 8252, the "client_secret" for native apps is not
# confidential — Google still issues one but it's embedded in
# every distributed binary. Treat it as identifying-but-not-secret.
#
# build.rs picks these up at compile time and forwards them via
# `cargo:rustc-env=...`; the running binary reads them via
# `option_env!()`. Changing .env triggers a rebuild.

GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=
